 "single_token_context": {
  "_about": "161 of the patterns are one bare token. A lone token is not specific enough on its own -- MERRILL GARDENS is a senior-living chain, MARCUS THEATRES is a cinema -- and a wordlist cannot separate the safe tokens from the unsafe ones, because MERRILL and VARO are names rather than words. So a single-token match is accepted only when the descriptor carries one of the context words below, or when nothing else is left after the corporate tail. Multi-token patterns are already specific and are not subject to this. Mirrors repair_competitors.pattern_is_usable, which applies the same rule to the competition dictionary.",
